    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/construction-project-manager-elon-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Construction Project Manager",
      "description": "Construction Project Manager - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Construction Project Manager - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Construction Project Manager position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Construction Project Manager Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Facilities University Operations Staff Full-Time Title: Construction Project Manager Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: M-F Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: Finance and Administration Department: Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. Location: Elon Campus Position Summary The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience Minimum of eight years of progressively responsible construction management experience delivering higher education, institutional, healthcare, or schedule driven projects. Experience must include substantial direct responsibility during construction for contractor management, schedule control, cost management, change management, field issue resolution, and project closeout. Bachelor's degree in engineering, architecture, construction management, or related field. Significant progressively responsible construction experience may substitute for formal education. Such as prior experience working for a construction company as a project manager, project engineer, superintendent, scheduler, or similar role requiring direct interaction with subcontractors. Preferred Education and Experience Bachelor's degree in construction management, engineering, architecture, or related field preferred. PMP certification a plus. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Mastery of design and construction process. Ability to read, understand and create construction drawings including Structural, Civil, Architectural, and MEP. Experience with AutoCAD, MS Word, MS Excel, Microsoft Project, and Procore. Required Other Training, Certifications, or Licensing FE, PE, PMP, NCARB, RA certification and/or general contractor license. Job Duties PROJECT MANAGEMENT Manage the construction, and close out phases as well as coordinate activities of designated projects to ensure that goals or objectives of project are accomplished within prescribed time fame and funding parameters. Perform the full range of project management cycle from bidding to close-out: initiating, planning, budgeting, executing, monitoring and controlling, and closing. Manage the construction budgets from conception through final completion. CONSTRUCTION MANAGEMENT Lead the University's construction-phase management of assigned projects and serve as the Owner's primary representative in managing contractor performance and successful project delivery. Monitor contractor performance against contractual schedule requirements, project milestones, and University occupancy commitments. Collaborate with contractors to develop and implement recovery plans when adjustments are needed to maintain project milestones. Review baseline schedules, schedule updates, critical path activities, procurement schedules, manpower and sequencing. Confirm reported progress is consistent with actual field conditions and challenge unsupported schedule assumptions or completion projections. Maintain a strong field presence and routinely evaluate construction progress, staffing, sequencing, quality, safety concerns, site logistics, and constraints that could affect project delivery. Facilitate constructive performance discussions with contractors by establishing clear expectations, documenting commitments, monitoring corrective actions, and supporting timely resolution of outstanding issues. Establish clear expectations, document commitments, track corrective actions, and escalate unresolved issues as appropriate. Anticipate construction risks and identify potential delays, conflicts, long-lead procurement issues, design conflicts or omissions, owner decisions, and other impediments before they affect the critical path. Lead construction progress meetings with a focus on decisions, accountability, schedule, outstanding RFIs/submittals, procurement, change management, and resolution of constraints. Review contractor payment applications and validate reported percent complete against actual work in place and contractual requirements. Review change order requests for entitlement, scope, cost, schedule impact, supporting documentation, and compliance with the contract. Negotiate or support negotiation of changes to protect the University's interests. Coordinate with architects, engineers, University stakeholders and authorities having jurisdiction to resolve field conditions and construction issues promptly. Oversee punch-list completion, commissioning, inspections, training, closeout documentation and warranty obligations and drive these activities to completion. DESIGN & PLANNING Reviews construction documents, bid packages, contracts for constructability and compliance with AIA owner-contractor contracts, and schedule. Reviews submitted bid packages and awarding contract to successful bidder. GENERAL ADMINISTRATION Attends departmental and division meetings Reviews and certifies invoices for payment Solicits estimates and establish purchase orders for goods and services. INCLUSIVE COMMUNITY BUILDING Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. **Special Instructions to Applicants: The search is being conducted by the Duffy Group. Please send all application materials including a resume and cover letter to the Duffy Group. Leslye Pas, Senior Recruiter/ lpas@duffygroup.com .** Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c1f9bda7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) a48104cb Last Name (required) 7d89a1aa Email (required) ecdc8f5a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university operations. The position also advances digital accessibility through resources, consultations, and support for accessible digital practices, and contributes to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular travel between the campuses of Queens University of Charlotte and Elon University’s South End (Charlotte) is expected. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events at Elon University’s campus in Elon, NC is expected. Research Associate in Insect Vibrational Communication Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon University and the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) are seeking a Research Associate with a background in animal communication to conduct exciting, cutting-edge research on the invasive spotted lanternfly (SLF) (Hemiptera: Lycorma delicatula). The ideal candidate would have expertise in the study of vibrational communication (i.e., biotremology) or acoustic communication. Research will focus on elucidating the role of SLF vibrational signals in insect mate selection behaviors, aggregation, and other behaviors that may be exploited as pest control methods. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a team to develop vibrational signals into stimuli for novel behavior-based Integrated Pest Management tools and publish results in peer-reviewed journals. This position will be stationed at the USDA-APHIS Forest Pest Methods Laboratory (FPML) located in Buzzards Bay, Massachusetts, working closely with Dr. Miriam Cooperband at USDA-APHIS, in collaboration with Dr. Jennifer Hamel at Elon University and Dr. Rodrigo Krugner at USDA-ARS. Most work would occur at FPML, but the successful candidate would also travel to Elon University up to twice a year for field work and opportunities related to an academic setting. This position will support the training and development of a researcher with interests in insect communication and applied research. The successful candidate would work among a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technicians at the USDA APHIS PPQ FPML, gain experience investigating practical, real-world entomological problems involving important invasive species of insects, within a biosecure facility and in the field, and would also have opportunities to gain faculty- and student-facing experiences in an academic setting when visiting Elon University. Annual salary of $84,579 (Doctoral degree) or $69,905 (Master’s degree). This 12-month appointment has the possibility of renewal for up to three years. Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager Human Resources Reporting to the Director of Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, the Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager plays a pivotal role in ensuring the University's compliance with relevant Civil Rights laws and regulations (Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, ADA/504), policies, and training, with a specific focus on promoting fostering an inclusive and diverse campus community through training, outreach, and case management. The Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager is responsible for developing and implementing strategies, programs, and training initiatives related to civil rights and compliance with applicable laws and guidelines. The manager maintains confidential student and employee files in the university’s databases and serves as primary intake person in response to reports of sexual assault, sexual harassment, stalking, dating and domestic violence, and all other protected categories of discrimination and harassment. The manager is highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities; strong critical thinking skills; the ability to exercise good judgment and high levels of discretion/confidentiality; an intense focus on accuracy; excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 85c3010e Last Name (required) 6b2fd517 Email (required) b47d605b Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
