    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/assistant-teaching-professor-in-sport-management-elon-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Sport Management",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Sport Management - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Assistant Teaching Professor in Sport Management - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Assistant Teaching Professor in Sport Management position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Assistant Teaching Professor in Sport Management Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Academic Affairs Faculty Full-Time Assistant Teaching Professor in Sport Management Department of Sport Management | School of Communications | Fall 2027 Position Summary The Department of Sport Management in Elon University’s School of Communications invites applications for a full-time Assistant Teaching Professor in Sport Management beginning the fall 2027 semester. This renewable, non-tenure-track position is eligible for promotion through the teaching professor ranks in accordance with university policy. The position is based on Elon’s campus in Elon, North Carolina, and requires regular on-campus presence. The successful candidate will teach seven undergraduate sport management courses per academic year, typically in a 3-1-3 distribution: three courses in the fall semester, one during Winter Term (a month-long academic term in January), and three in the spring semester. Classes are held in person, either M-W-F for 70 minutes or Tu-Th or M-W for 100 minutes. Additional responsibilities include advising and mentoring undergraduate majors and/or student organizations, providing professional service to the department, school and university, and contributing actively to the life of the institution. As a teacher-scholar-mentor, the successful candidate will place excellent teaching, meaningful student relationships, and engaged learning at the center of their work. Teaching may include Contemporary Sport Management, Sport Data and Research, Sport Marketing, Sport Law, Sport Media, Sport Finance, Event and Venue Management, and courses in the Elon Core Curriculum. Other elective courses can be taught and developed. Candidates who have experience working with a diverse range of people, and who can contribute to the climate of inclusivity are encouraged to identify their experiences in their cover letter. Minimum Qualifications A master’s degree in Sport Management or another advanced degree in a closely related field by the date of appointment. The ability to teach undergraduate sport management courses. Preferred Qualifications An earned doctorate in Sport Management or a closely related field. Evidence of high-quality teaching and professional development at the college level. Professional experience in the sport industry. Application Process Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by Monday, October 26, will be assured of consideration. Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vita, teaching statement and research statement. Department of Sport Management The Department of Sport Management at Elon University prepares students for the business of sport, including professional sport, intercollegiate athletics, recreation, events, facilities, and sport-related organizations. The curriculum combines a liberal arts foundation with industry-focused coursework in leadership, marketing, finance, communication, law, research, analytics, event management, and contemporary issues in sport. Students benefit from small classes, close faculty mentorship, internships, undergraduate research, academic service learning, special events, study away, and other engaged-learning opportunities. The department is accredited by the Commission on Sport Management Accreditation (COSMA) and maintains strong connections with alumni and professionals across the sport industry. School of Communications Established in 2000, Elon University’s School of Communications inspires graduates to be thought leaders committed to the public good in today’s rapidly evolving landscape of digital communications. Teacher-scholar-mentors with decades of collective professional experience educate students across seven majors: cinema & television arts, digital content management, journalism, media analytics, sport management, strategic communications and visual communication. The School of Communications is home to approximately 1,100 students and more than 70 faculty and staff, all centered around a 105,000-square-foot quad that functions as a dynamic learning laboratory. Facilities feature state-of-the-art television studios, video editing suites, classrooms and faculty offices, a movie theater, and a virtual studio with an xR (extended reality) wall. Elon University Elon University is a nationally recognized leader in engaged, experiential learning that prepares graduates to be creative, resilient, ambitious and ethical citizens of our global culture. At Elon, more than 7,000 students learn through hands-on experiences and close working relationships with faculty and staff whose priorities are teaching and mentoring. The Elon curriculum is grounded in the traditional liberal arts and sciences with an emphasis on global experiences and career development. More than 80 undergraduate majors are complemented by professional and graduate programs in law, business, education and healthcare. Elon is ranked among the best national universities by U.S. News & World Report, with a No. 1 ranking for excellence in undergraduate teaching for five consecutive years. In addition, Elon is the only university recognized in the Top 10 of all eight categories of programs that enhance the student experience, including internships, learning communities and first-year experiences. To learn more, visit Elon University . Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert be05bdeb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Communications School of Communications Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) f862b1d0 Last Name (required) be92595f Email (required) 3f00eae9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university operations. The position also advances digital accessibility through resources, consultations, and support for accessible digital practices, and contributes to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular travel between the campuses of Queens University of Charlotte and Elon University’s South End (Charlotte) is expected. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events at Elon University’s campus in Elon, NC is expected. Research Associate in Insect Vibrational Communication Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon University and the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) are seeking a Research Associate with a background in animal communication to conduct exciting, cutting-edge research on the invasive spotted lanternfly (SLF) (Hemiptera: Lycorma delicatula). The ideal candidate would have expertise in the study of vibrational communication (i.e., biotremology) or acoustic communication. Research will focus on elucidating the role of SLF vibrational signals in insect mate selection behaviors, aggregation, and other behaviors that may be exploited as pest control methods. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a team to develop vibrational signals into stimuli for novel behavior-based Integrated Pest Management tools and publish results in peer-reviewed journals. This position will be stationed at the USDA-APHIS Forest Pest Methods Laboratory (FPML) located in Buzzards Bay, Massachusetts, working closely with Dr. Miriam Cooperband at USDA-APHIS, in collaboration with Dr. Jennifer Hamel at Elon University and Dr. Rodrigo Krugner at USDA-ARS. Most work would occur at FPML, but the successful candidate would also travel to Elon University up to twice a year for field work and opportunities related to an academic setting. This position will support the training and development of a researcher with interests in insect communication and applied research. The successful candidate would work among a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technicians at the USDA APHIS PPQ FPML, gain experience investigating practical, real-world entomological problems involving important invasive species of insects, within a biosecure facility and in the field, and would also have opportunities to gain faculty- and student-facing experiences in an academic setting when visiting Elon University. Annual salary of $84,579 (Doctoral degree) or $69,905 (Master’s degree). This 12-month appointment has the possibility of renewal for up to three years. Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager Human Resources Reporting to the Director of Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, the Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager plays a pivotal role in ensuring the University's compliance with relevant Civil Rights laws and regulations (Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, ADA/504), policies, and training, with a specific focus on promoting fostering an inclusive and diverse campus community through training, outreach, and case management. The Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager is responsible for developing and implementing strategies, programs, and training initiatives related to civil rights and compliance with applicable laws and guidelines. The manager maintains confidential student and employee files in the university’s databases and serves as primary intake person in response to reports of sexual assault, sexual harassment, stalking, dating and domestic violence, and all other protected categories of discrimination and harassment. The manager is highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities; strong critical thinking skills; the ability to exercise good judgment and high levels of discretion/confidentiality; an intense focus on accuracy; excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) ac7f8ce7 Last Name (required) c156a240 Email (required) 09efb814 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website use