    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/principal-faculty-member-department-of-physician-assistant-studies-charlotte-elon-charlotte-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies - Charlotte - Elon",
      "description": "Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies - Charlotte - Elon - Charlotte Campus, North Carolina, United States Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies - Charlotte - Elon - Charlotte Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies - Charlotte position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies - Charlotte Elon - Charlotte Campus, North Carolina, 28208 Academic Affairs Faculty Full-Time Title: Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies - Charlotte Position Type: Faculty Full-Time VP Area: Office of the Provost and Academic Affairs Department: School of Health Sciences Location: Elon - Charlotte Campus Position Summary Elon University, renowned as a model for engaged learning, invites applications and nominations for a Principal Faculty position in the new Elon Physician Assistant Studies Program in Charlotte. Elon University is seeking a full-time Principal Faculty member to join the founding team of the developing Physician Assistant (PA) program within the Department of Physician Assistant Studies in Charlotte. This individual will play a central role in the launch, delivery, and continuous improvement of the program, with primary responsibilities spanning course development, instructional design, assessment strategy, and student success. The successful candidate will develop courses within the approved curriculum, build and manage course content within the learning management system and create and implement high-quality assessments, including exam construction and deployment. This faculty member will actively engage in teaching, student mentorship, and academic advising, contributing to a supportive and outcomes-driven learning environment. In addition, the faculty member will support programmatic assessment and accreditation efforts, including data collection, analysis, and reporting aligned with ARC-PA standards. This includes contributing to the Self-Study Report (SSR), ongoing outcomes tracking, and preparation for the program’s continued accreditation review following graduation of the inaugural cohort. The role also includes collaboration in curriculum evaluation and refinement, participation in faculty governance, and engagement with community and clinical partners to support the program’s mission and student learning experiences. This PA program is part of the Elon University’s School of Health Sciences (SHS), which currently includes an existing Department of Physician Assistant Studies program established in 2012, a Doctor of Physical Therapy program established in 1998, and Department of Nursing program established in 2021, located in Elon, NC. Additionally, a Clinical mental Health Counseling program launched this year, with cohorts in Elon and in Charlotte. Principal faculty report directly to the Founding Chair/Program Director. The appointment for this position will be either tenure track, contingent on eligibility, or an ongoing, non-tenure track line. The compensation offered will be commensurate with qualifications and include an excellent benefits package and generous retirement plan. Responsibilities: • Assist in the development of the program and contribute to support of accreditation compliance with ARC-PA. • Direct academic courses o Coordinate the sequencing and delivery of content within assigned courses in the didactic and clinical year. o Coordinate the implementation of student evaluation within these courses. • Serve as lecturer, lab instructor, small group facilitator, and evaluator in assigned didactic and clinical phase courses; lecture in other courses according to subject matter expertise. • Demonstrate excellence and innovation in teaching while proactively addressing the evolving needs of the program and its students. • Establish and foster relationships with clinical partners and preceptors to support student training. • Support and engage in admissions activities. • Participate in recruitment activities and represent the program at community events. • Assist with other departmental responsibilities such as proctoring exams, grading OSCEs, interviewing admissions candidates, etc. • Serve as Scholarly Project advisor. • Advise and provide academic counseling for students in both the academic and clinical phases. • Serve on departmental, School of Health Sciences, and University committees as elected or appointed. • Support the admissions process through applicant review, records tracking, process improvement initiatives, and service on the program-level Admissions Committee. • Maintain a record of ongoing scholarly activity and faculty development. • Assist with program self-assessment and improvement. • Perform other duties as assigned by the Program Director. Benefits of Working at Elon About Elon University: Elon University is the nationally recognized leader in engaged, experiential learning that prepares graduates to be creative, resilient, ambitious and ethical citizens of our global culture. With a deliberate emphasis on exceptional teaching and experiential learning, students engage with mentors and peers who bridge the gap between knowledge and its transformative impact. This North Carolina university was recently honored to be ranked among the top universities in the nation by US News & World Report, receiving a #1 ranking for undergraduate teaching and a #13 ranking for \"most innovative\" University. The University is comprised of six schools that serve a selective student body of over 7,000. Elon is one of only seven private universities in the country with accredited schools of business, communications, education, law, and health sciences, plus a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa, the nation's oldest and most prestigious academic honor society. About Charlotte, North Carolina: Charlotte is one of the 20 largest cities in the U.S. and the largest city in North Carolina. Home to over 900,000 residents, it offers a vibrant blend of Southern charm and urban appeal, with a strong focus on housing development, community safety, efficient transportation, economic growth, and environmental sustainability. The city hosts more than 10 Fortune 1000 companies, such as Bank of America, Lowe’s, and Duke Energy, making it a major financial and business hub. Residents enjoy a rich cultural scene with museums, theaters, and the historic Uptown district. Sports fans can enjoy the Carolina Panthers, Charlotte Hornets, and Charlotte FC, or visit the NASCAR Hall of Fame. Outdoor enthusiasts have access to the U.S. National Whitewater Center and extensive greenways and parks. With its diverse job market, affordable cost of living, and variety of amenities, Charlotte is an attractive city for professionals and families alike. Minimum Required Education and Experience Qualifications: • Terminal degree in physician assistant studies or equivalent professional degree in a relevant healthcare discipline combined with educational experience. • Prior teaching experience in higher education or health professions education strongly preferred. • Demonstrated clinical experience (minimum of three years strongly preferred). • Excellent written and oral communication skills. • Evidence of commitment to collaboration, innovation, and supporting student success. • Familiarity with, or willingness to learn, learning management systems (LMS), Canvas, ExamSoft, Exxat, VH Dissector, and related educational technology. • Proficiency with general office technology (e.g., Microsoft Office Suite). Special Instructions to Applicants: All correspondence relating to the principal faculty position at Elon University-Charlotte should be directed in confidence to Lindsay Waddell: lwaddell3@elon.edu A complete application should include the following: Cover Letter outlining your interest and qualifications for the position, Updated CV, List of three (3) professional references with contact information, title, institutional affiliation, email address and direct phone numbers. Applications received by October 12, 2026, will receive priority consideration. Review of applications will begin immediately and will be rolling until filled. We strongly encourage candidates with experience engaging diverse populations and fostering an inclusive environment to highlight these contributions in their cover letter. The anticipated start date is January 2027. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert e89a7283 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Health Sciences School of Health Sciences Locations Elon - Charlotte Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon - Charlotte Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 50109783 Last Name (required) 985fd9c1 Email (required) 2fdca943 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university operations. The position also advances digital accessibility through resources, consultations, and support for accessible digital practices, and contributes to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular travel between the campuses of Queens University of Charlotte and Elon University’s South End (Charlotte) is expected. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events at Elon University’s campus in Elon, NC is expected. Research Associate in Insect Vibrational Communication Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon University and the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) are seeking a Research Associate with a background in animal communication to conduct exciting, cutting-edge research on the invasive spotted lanternfly (SLF) (Hemiptera: Lycorma delicatula). The ideal candidate would have expertise in the study of vibrational communication (i.e., biotremology) or acoustic communication. Research will focus on elucidating the role of SLF vibrational signals in insect mate selection behaviors, aggregation, and other behaviors that may be exploited as pest control methods. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a team to develop vibrational signals into stimuli for novel behavior-based Integrated Pest Management tools and publish results in peer-reviewed journals. This position will be stationed at the USDA-APHIS Forest Pest Methods Laboratory (FPML) located in Buzzards Bay, Massachusetts, working closely with Dr. Miriam Cooperband at USDA-APHIS, in collaboration with Dr. Jennifer Hamel at Elon University and Dr. Rodrigo Krugner at USDA-ARS. Most work would occur at FPML, but the successful candidate would also travel to Elon University up to twice a year for field work and opportunities related to an academic setting. This position will support the training and development of a researcher with interests in insect communication and applied research. The successful candidate would work among a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technicians at the USDA APHIS PPQ FPML, gain experience investigating practical, real-world entomological problems involving important invasive species of insects, within a biosecure facility and in the field, and would also have opportunities to gain faculty- and student-facing experiences in an academic setting when visiting Elon University. Annual salary of $84,579 (Doctoral degree) or $69,905 (Master’s degree). This 12-month appointment has the possibility of renewal for up to three years. Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager Human Resources Reporting to the Director of Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, the Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager plays a pivotal role in ensuring the University's compliance with relevant Civil Rights laws and regulations (Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, ADA/504), policies, and training, with a specific focus on promoting fostering an inclusive and diverse campus community through training, outreach, and case management. The Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager is responsible for developing and implementing strategies, programs, and training initiatives related to civil rights and compliance with applicable laws and guidelines. The manager maintains confidential student and employee files in the university’s databases and serves as primary intake person in response to reports of sexual assault, sexual harassment, stalking, dating and domestic violence, and all other protected categories of discrimination and harassment. The manager is highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities; strong critical thinking skills; the ability to exercise good judgment and high levels of discretion/confidentiality; an intense focus on accuracy; excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 2b2806be Last Name (required) c4965e87 Email (required) 9dea03b1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/director-of-alumni-engagement-queens-queens-campus-charlotte-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens - Queens Campus",
      "description": "Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens - Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens - Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, 28216 Advancement Services Staff Full-Time Title: Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Monday - Friday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: University Advancement Department: University Advancement Location: Queens Campus - Charlotte Position Summary Reporting to the Senior Director of Alumni Engagement, the Director of Alumni Engagement, Queens is responsible for planning, implementing, and managing Queens alumni engagement opportunities. The director serves a critical role as ambassador for the University, building strong and sustained relationships with all undergraduate and graduate alumni and engaging them in meaningful ways through communications, experiences, volunteerism and philanthropy. Benefits of Working at Elon Community is foundational to Queens and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Queens should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Queens’ foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Queens. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Queens community. Minimum Required Education and Experience • Requires a bachelor’s degree from a four-year college or university. Experience in higher education preferred. • Seven to ten years professional experience in sales, marketing, communications, events, customer service and/or volunteer management preferred; or equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Education and Experience Preference will be given to applicants who are alumni of Queens University of Charlotte. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Excellent interpersonal and communication skills (verbal, written, presentation), including exemplary poise, tact and diplomacy when working with a wide range of constituents and diverse audiences. • Proven ability to lead, develop and support team members to achieve delivery of high-quality programs and fundraising initiatives by providing meaningful and motivating coaching, training and feedback. • Strong reasoning skills and the ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, draw valid conclusions, and make well-thought-through recommendations • A desire to grapple with complex systems and to simplify and improve intricate processes. • Preferred experience in project management in similar roles. • Demonstrated competence with technology, with preference given to applicants who are familiar with Slate for Advancement, social media, and other commonly used Advancement platforms. • Demonstrated organization and planning skills (strategic, short- and long-term); strong follow-up and follow-through skills to ensure achievement of strategic plans, goals and objectives. • Strong reasoning skills and the ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, draw valid conclusions, and make well-thought-through recommendations. • Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment and to effectively prioritize assignments to meet given deadlines. Job Duties Foster lasting relationships between the University and its constituents and establish a structured, systematic program of engagement opportunities that will ensure ongoing, meaningful relationships with students, alumni and donors. Hold a portfolio of leadership annual giving prospects. Lead volunteer committees in the planning of milestone and affinity reunion events as well as planning the logistics and programmatic pieces of reunion that all classes attend. Coordinate with volunteers in key cities to support events and local members of the Queens community that support pride and philanthropy for the College. Support giving day activities such as Giving Tuesday and QUnited through identifying alumni advocates, completing their training and providing day of support. Develop relationships through scheduled meetings with key volunteer leaders on the Alumni Association Board. In collaboration with the executive committee, plan annual meetings. Lead the Homecoming committee, comprised of students, alumni and staff in planning the week of activities including but not limited to invitations, programmatic schedule of events and fanfest. Lead the development of alumni affinity programming to extend engagement opportunities for alumni constituents. Community is foundational to Queens and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Queens should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Queens’ foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Queens. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Queens community. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1c3fca79 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Locations Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 8e7f1776 Last Name (required) 877116a4 Email (required) b0e3c706 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university op