    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/club-sports-coach-men-s-lacrosse-elon-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Club Sports Coach-Men's Lacrosse",
      "description": "Club Sports Coach-Men's Lacrosse - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Club Sports Coach-Men's Lacrosse - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Club Sports Coach-Men's Lacrosse position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Club Sports Coach-Men's Lacrosse Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Athletics Staff Part-Time Title: Club Sports Coach-Men's Lacrosse Position Type: Staff Part-Time Days Per Week: Varies based on practice and game schedules VP Area: Student Life Department: Campus Recreation Location: Elon Campus Position Summary The Head Coach for Men’s Club Lacrosse is a member of the Campus Recreation staff in the Division of Student Life and serves as the primary coach and leader for the program. Club sports teams at Elon are student organizations, run by student leaders who manage many aspects of organization operations. Club sports programs promote student development, engaging co-curricular experiences, high-level athletic competition, and positive representation of the university. As part of a broader initiative to advance club sports at the university, the Men's Club Lacrosse Head Coach will serve as the team coach, coordinate administrative aspects of program operations, work closely with Admissions to recruit student athletes (in coordination with Admissions), and achieve important fundraising goals (in coordination with University Advancement). This position requires evening and weekend work. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Elon is proud to have been named to the list of Most Promising Places to Work in Student Affairs each of the past six years. For additional information about working with the Division of Student Life, Visit: https://www.elon.edu/u/administration/student-life/about/work-with-us/ Minimum Required Education and Experience Requires rules knowledge and regulations of league and requirements. Previous experience as a player or coach. Job Duties Coaching Manage and supervise sport activities, contests, and practice sessions to promote individual growth in athletic skills, teamwork, and good sportsmanship. Use a variety of instructional techniques and media to meet the needs and improve the abilities of student athletes in the sport assigned. Work with the members of the club to plan and put in place instructional goals and objectives to ensure the overall development of student athletes whose abilities range from beginner to experienced. Administrative Responsible for coordinating home and away competitions as well as tournaments. Communication with constituents, parents/alumni, athletic trainer, club sports department, and vendors to ensure team is well supported. Perform other duties as assigned by the Assistant Director for Competitive Sports. Recruiting and Fundraising Partner with Admissions to recruit student athletes and meet established targets for team size. Assist the team in fundraising efforts throughout the year, in coordination with University Advancement. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert fa2c32f8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Campus Recreation Campus Recreation Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) b5a297c8 Last Name (required) 84b23499 Email (required) 5dc94ca0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible fo