    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-music-and-director-of-bands-elon-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Bands",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Bands - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Bands - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Bands position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Bands Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Academic Affairs Faculty Full-Time Title: Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Bands Position Type: Faculty Full-Time VP Area: Office of the Provost and Academic Affairs Department: Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Location: Elon Campus Position Summary Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Bands position in the Department of Music, beginning July 2027. This position offers an exciting opportunity to shape and grow an athletic band program within a Division I university while contributing to the musical and educational environment of a nationally recognized residential liberal arts institution. The primary responsibility of the position is the leadership and development of Elon’s athletic bands, including the Fire of the Carolinas Marching Band and pep band, in close and sustained partnership with the Department of Athletics. Responsibilities will include hiring and supervising student and instructional staff; developing student leadership structures; managing inventory and equipment; overseeing budgets; and coordinating rehearsals, performances, travel, and other program activities. Additional responsibilities will include conducting the Wind Ensemble and/or Concert Band and may include teaching other courses, including in the Core Curriculum, based on the needs of the Department of Music and the candidate’s expertise. The successful candidate will bring a clear vision for advancing the musical, educational, and public profile of Elon’s athletic and concert bands and for building an engaging band program that attracts and retains students from across the university while strengthening the Department of Music’s degree programs. The successful candidate will demonstrate strong conducting and rehearsal skills; effective communication and organizational abilities; the ability to collaborate with students, faculty, staff, Athletics, Admissions, alumni, donors, and other university partners; and effective recruitment strategies for the band and Department of Music. These efforts should include building positive relationships with prospective students, families, and secondary-school music educators. Candidates are encouraged to identify their experiences in contributing to a climate of inclusivity in their cover letters. Elon is a dynamic private, co-educational, comprehensive institution that is a national model for actively engaging faculty and students in teaching and learning in a liberal arts based residential campus. To learn more about Elon, please visit the University website at www.elon.edu. Benefits of Working at Elon Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences, and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, decisions related to hiring, compensating, training, evaluating performance, are made fairly, and we provide equal employment opportunities to all qualified candidates and employees. At Elon we strive to follow our mission, where our employees are empowered to respect human differences, have a passion for lifelong learning, an emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Additional Information: To support Elon’s teacher-scholar-mentor model, we offer an attractive package of research support than includes a pre-tenure sabbatical, course reassignment times, summer research grants, and funds for conference travel Minimum Required Education and Experience DMA in Music must be completed prior to the start of employment. Preferred Education and Experience Experience directing collegiate bands, including marching and pep bands. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please attach letter of application, CV, teaching statement, statement of research interests, and contact information for three references. Semi-finalists will be asked to provide a video of recent band rehearsal and/or performance. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Complete applications must be received by October 23, 2026, to be assured of consideration. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 2aba541b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) fc483b94 Last Name (required) 91d49ab7 Email (required) 1d04daef Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas 