    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-alumni-engagement-initiatives-elon-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement Initiatives",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement Initiatives - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement Initiatives - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement Initiatives position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement Initiatives Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Advancement Services Staff Full-Time Title: Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement Initiatives Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Monday - Friday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: University Advancement Department: University Advancement Location: Elon Campus Position Summary Reporting to the Senior Director of Alumni Engagement, the Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement Initiatives is responsible for developing and executing the strategic vision of Elon’s alumni relationship cultivation and stewardship, volunteerism and professional development efforts. The Assistant Director is responsible for building relationships with Elon alumni to engage them in activities that will enhance the future of our university. This position will design a strategic approach to identify, cultivate, and steward our alumni as partners, advocates, and investors. This position will communicate with the alumni body regularly via the monthly alumni newsletter and Elon alumni social media accounts. In addition, the Assistant Director of Alumni Engagement Initiatives will provide leadership of advancement’s alumni professional engagement efforts including, but not limited to, in-person and virtual professional development, networking opportunities and lifelong learning programs/events. The Assistant Director, in coordination with other colleagues and units across campus, will help develop, build and promote a variety of programming for alumni both on and off campus plus virtually. In addition, the Assistant Director will be responsible for managing a menu of alumni volunteer opportunities and promoting them to the alumni body. In conjunction with other members of the Alumni Engagement team, the Assistant Director will identify and recruit alumni volunteers and inspire excitement for opportunities. This position will also develop and implement a program of communication with alumni who have completed volunteer roles to inspire future and continued engagement. The person in this position is expected to be a key leader within the Alumni Engagement team and play a vital role in helping University Advancement achieve its engagement goals. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience Requires bachelor's degree from a four-year college or university or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Education and Experience Master's degree is a plus and three to five years professional/internship experience in sales, marketing, communications, events, customer service and/or volunteer management preferred but not required. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Position requires the ability to and experience with making presentations to various groups of constituencies. Additionally, the position requires the ability to meet face to face with all levels of constituents and ability to handle constituent complaints. The position requires the ability to work effectively as a team member, work on multiple projects, possess strong leadership, organization, and customer relations skills. Job Duties Connecting with alumni based on Advancement university priorities through email, social media, mailings, phone calls, and face to face meetings either at Elon or in alumni cities of residence. Coordinate and facilitate online webinars, workshops, content and digital resources. Develop and cultivate partnership(s) with on-campus departments and programs focused on career services and professional development opportunities (SPDC, OLPD, etc.) to highlight existing opportunities and build new programs in partnership. Collaborate with University Advancement communications team to manage engagement communications, professional development content and alumni volunteer opportunity promotion using existing platforms such as lifelongelon.com, LinkedIn, monthly newsletter and other social media channels. Identifying alumni as for volunteers and board prospects for roles including: Elon Alumni Board, Young Alumni Council, President's Advisory Council, LSB, Communications Advisory Board, National Advisory Board for School of Education, reunion, affinity and class committees, etc. Serve as the liaison for the Young Alumni Council. Assisting with Elon events including Senior Class Giving, Homecoming, reunions, Family Weekend, Evenings for Elon, Cheers to Elon, Elon Day, Alumni Awards Weekend, Commencement, chapter activities, athletic events, etc. Providing exceptional customer service to our alumni acting with the greatest amount of professionalism and expressing the highest sense of urgency. Actively enhancing professional development by participating in educational opportunities; reading professional publications; attending appropriate conferences; building relationships with colleagues at Elon and other institutions; etc. Inclusive Community Building Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert d1d57052 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) cefc99e8 Last Name (required) 1690d639 Email (required) 979f89f4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university operations. The position also advances digital accessibility through resources, consultations, and support for accessible digital practices, and contributes to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular travel between the campuses of Queens University of Charlotte and Elon University’s South End (Charlotte) is expected. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events at Elon University’s campus in Elon, NC is expected. Research Associate in Insect Vibrational Communication Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon University and the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) are seeking a Research Associate with a background in animal communication to conduct exciting, cutting-edge research on the invasive spotted lanternfly (SLF) (Hemiptera: Lycorma delicatula). The ideal candidate would have expertise in the study of vibrational communication (i.e., biotremology) or acoustic communication. Research will focus on elucidating the role of SLF vibrational signals in insect mate selection behaviors, aggregation, and other behaviors that may be exploited as pest control methods. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a team to develop vibrational signals into stimuli for novel behavior-based Integrated Pest Management tools and publish results in peer-reviewed journals. This position will be stationed at the USDA-APHIS Forest Pest Methods Laboratory (FPML) located in Buzzards Bay, Massachusetts, working closely with Dr. Miriam Cooperband at USDA-APHIS, in collaboration with Dr. Jennifer Hamel at Elon University and Dr. Rodrigo Krugner at USDA-ARS. Most work would occur at FPML, but the successful candidate would also travel to Elon University up to twice a year for field work and opportunities related to an academic setting. This position will support the training and development of a researcher with interests in insect communication and applied research. The successful candidate would work among a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technicians at the USDA APHIS PPQ FPML, gain experience investigating practical, real-world entomological problems involving important invasive species of insects, within a biosecure facility and in the field, and would also have opportunities to gain faculty- and student-facing experiences in an academic setting when visiting Elon University. Annual salary of $84,579 (Doctoral degree) or $69,905 (Master’s degree). This 12-month appointment has the possibility of renewal for up to three years. Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager Human Resources Reporting to the Director of Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, the Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager plays a pivotal role in ensuring the University's compliance with relevant Civil Rights laws and regulations (Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, ADA/504), policies, and training, with a specific focus on promoting fostering an inclusive and diverse campus community through training, outreach, and case management. The Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager is responsible for developing and implementing strategies, programs, and training initiatives related to civil rights and compliance with applicable laws and guidelines. The manager maintains confidential student and employee files in the university’s databases and serves as primary intake person in response to reports of sexual assault, sexual harassment, stalking, dating and domestic violence, and all other protected categories of discrimination and harassment. The manager is highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities; strong critical thinking skills; the ability to exercise good judgment and high levels of discretion/confidentiality; an intense focus on accuracy; excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 18de97e6 Last Name (required) 2fea94da Email (required) 11e5e08e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
