      "description": "Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 University Administration Staff Full-Time Title: Program Assistant - Exercise Science, Neuroscience, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: M-F Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: Office of the Provost and Academic Affairs Department: Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary Position involves the performance of a variety of administrative, clerical, and office management duties. Position requires knowledge of College and University policies and procedures to communicate information involving academic programs, functions, and services. Duties performed include using office technology to compile presentations, records, and reports; organizing, maintaining, and distributing information from the office to other units on campus; and greeting/referring/assisting visitors/faculty/staff/others. Completion of work often involves serving as office representative in obtaining, clarifying, and providing information about programs in the College. Position serves as the primary staff assistant to the Chair(s), Program Directors, Dean(s) and faculty in the department(s) and the College. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience High School Diploma and minimum of 2 years of experience in an office or related environment. Job Duties Provide front office support to the Units represented Maintain the Unit's calendar/schedule, anticipate annual cycle of required meetings and reports across academic year and ensure that the Chair completes those items in a timely manner Maintain the faculty, staff, and department digital records (annual reports, assessment reports, and external reviews for the department) Maintain strict confidentiality related to personnel and student needs Assist faculty, as needed, in summarizing department level reports On board new faculty and staff within the Unit, including training and meetings with key offices Event planning and communication for Unit office(s) (e.g., faculty meetings, graduation events, etc.) Support University Communications liaison to the College in maintenance of the Unit webpages Reflects a unified voice of the College in the operations and communications with other offices on campus and throughout higher education. Train and supervise student workers within the Unit's office Inclusive Community Building Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert d7ff9561 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) ffc7bd0c Last Name (required) 8e0ccad3 Email (required) c4a9d074 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles o