    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/principal-faculty-member-department-of-physician-assistant-studies-elon-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states-0bd5fc7b-2cd4-4f8f-a2a1-b76da59c0339": {
      "title": "Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon",
      "description": "Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Principal Faculty Member Department of Physician Assistant Studies Elon Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Academic Affairs Faculty Full-Time Principal Faculty Members Elon University , in partnership with the national search firm Scott Healy & Associates , invites applications and nominations for the position of Principal Faculty Member in the Department of Physician Assistant (PA) Studies. Elon University is accepting applications from experienced physician assistants to join its growing Physician Assistant Program at an exciting moment in the Department’s development. This position is tenure-track eligible. As the program plans to double its cohort size to meet the increasing demand for highly prepared PAs, Elon is seeking several new Principal Faculty members who want to contribute to a thriving and fully accredited program that is building on its strong foundation of success. Established in 2013, the program has continued to grow in reputation and impact, and this expansion reflects both the excellence of the current program and the University’s continued commitment to engaged, forward-thinking health sciences education. These full-time, twelve-month faculty roles offer several possible start dates, with positions beginning in summer or fall of 2026 and the winter of 2027. Principal Faculty report directly to the Chair/Program Director and play a key part in shaping curriculum, teaching across the didactic and clinical phases, and supporting students as teacher-scholar-mentors. Elon’s physician assistant faculty are encouraged to engage in clinical practice or scholarship one day each week. For educators who value meaningful student interaction, a supportive academic community, and the chance to contribute to a program that continues to grow in exciting ways, Elon University offers an exceptional professional home. The compensation offered will be commensurate with qualifications and include an excellent benefits package and generous retirement plan. Responsibilities: Demonstrate excellence and innovation in teaching. Direct academic courses: Coordinate the sequencing and delivery of content within assigned courses in the didactic and clinical year. Coordinate student evaluation within assigned courses. Serve as lecturer, lab instructor, small group facilitator and evaluator in didactic and clinical phase courses. With the support of the program, proactively address the evolving needs of the program and its students. Participate in other departmental responsibilities: Proctoring exams, grading OSCEs, facilitating case-based simulation activities, etc. Serve as Master’s Project advisor. Advise and provide academic counseling for students in academic and clinical phases, including conducting clinical site visits. Engage in admissions activities, including, but not limited to reviewing candidate applications, interviewing candidates, and selecting the cohort. Assist with program continuous self-assessment and improvement, including the ongoing evolution of the program and continuance of accreditation by ARC-PA. Serve on departmental, School of Health Science, and University committees as elected or appointed. Maintain a record of ongoing scholarly activity and faculty development. Timely completion of assigned tasks. Perform other duties as assigned by the Program Director. Qualifications: Terminal degree in PA studies or other applicable healthcare discipline. Current certification by the NCCPA or appropriate certifying board. Eligibility for North Carolina state licensure as appropriate. Minimum of 3 years of clinical experience. Teaching experience strongly preferred. Exceptional written and oral communication skills. Proficiency with educational and office technology (e.g., Microsoft Office Suite). About Elon University: Elon University is a selective, mid-sized private university renowned nationally as a model for engaged and experiential learning. Located in central North Carolina, the University is recognized as one of the nation's most beautiful collegiate environments. Students work closely with faculty who are teacher-scholar-mentors. The curriculum is grounded in the traditional liberal arts and sciences and complemented by nationally accredited professional and graduate programs. With a focus on teaching and student success, Elon was recently honored to be ranked among the top universities in the nation by US News & World Report, receiving a #1 ranking for undergraduate teaching and a #13 ranking for \"most innovative\" University. The University is comprised of six schools that serve a selective student body of over 6,000. Elon is one of only seven private universities in the country with accredited schools of business, communications, education, law, and health sciences, plus a chapter of Phi Beta Kappa, the nation's oldest and most prestigious academic honor society. About the School of Health Sciences: The School of Health Sciences was established in 2011 and includes graduate programs in Physical Therapy and Physician Assistant Studies in addition to the four-year Bachelor of Science in Nursing and Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing. The School of Health Sciences is located in the Francis Center, a state-of-the-art teaching and research facility near the main campus. Faculty, staff, and students in all programs collaborate on innovative research initiatives in interdisciplinary laboratories. The Interprofessional Simulation Center is a hub of experiential learning, allowing students to hone their skills in providing individualized care at the bedside, in the clinic, in the home, and in the community. About the Department of Physician Assistant Studies: The Department of Physician Assistant Studies , offered through the School of Health Sciences, prepares graduates to think critically and act skillfully to meet expanding health care needs in local and global communities. Students are immersed in a curriculum structured around active learning strategies through collaborative work with faculty, scholars and practitioners in the field. The 24-month program prepares graduates to employ the most current knowledge to care for patients’ physical, emotional and spiritual needs and advance health care equity. It is an exciting time within the department as the University looks to expand its faculty. About the Community: Elon, North Carolina , exudes a unique charm that captivates both residents and visitors alike. Nestled in the heart of the state, this delightful town of about 11,000 residents is a perfect blend of small-town warmth and progressive energy. With its tree-lined streets, historic downtown area, and welcoming community, Elon is renowned for its excellent schools, fostering a culture of learning and growth. Its vibrant arts scene, local boutiques, and diverse dining options contribute to a rich tapestry of experiences. Nature enthusiasts find solace in the nearby parks, walking trails, and nature reserves, and community events bring residents together throughout the year. Elon is truly a hidden gem of North Carolina. Elon’s location also offers the perfect balance between small-town charm and access to larger metropolitan areas. The town is conveniently situated near Greensboro , Raleigh , and Durham , making it easy to enjoy the cultural, professional, and recreational opportunities these cities offer. Charlotte , about 100 miles away, is a major draw with its thriving financial sector, professional sports teams, world-class dining, and vibrant arts and entertainment scene. This central location makes Elon an ideal spot for both work and leisure. Application and Nomination Process: All correspondence relating to the position of Principal Faculty Member at Elon University should be directed in confidence to the University’s executive search consultant: Dr. Lea Johnson, Assistant Vice President Scott Healy & Associates lea@scotthealy.com A complete application should include the following: Cover Letter outlining your interest and qualifications for the position; Updated CV; Contact information for three (3) professional references with title, institutional affiliation, email address and direct phone numbers. (No references will be contacted without written permission from the candidate.) Applications are being reviewed on a rolling basis. The search will remain open until the positions are filled. Elon University is an equal opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff and student body and welcomes all applicants. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert f34d3efa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Health Sciences School of Health Sciences Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) e4c076c3 Last Name (required) 4b4dda1b Email (required) e59edcc7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university operations. The position also advances digital accessibility through resources, consultations, and support for accessible digital practices, and contributes to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular travel between the campuses of Queens University of Charlotte and Elon University’s South End (Charlotte) is expected. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events at Elon University’s campus in Elon, NC is expected. Research Associate in Insect Vibrational Communication Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon University and the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) are seeking a Research Associate with a background in animal communication to conduct exciting, cutting-edge research on the invasive spotted lanternfly (SLF) (Hemiptera: Lycorma delicatula). The ideal candidate would have expertise in the study of vibrational communication (i.e., biotremology) or acoustic communication. Research will focus on elucidating the role of SLF vibrational signals in insect mate selection behaviors, aggregation, and other behaviors that may be exploited as pest control methods. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a team to develop vibrational signals into stimuli for novel behavior-based Integrated Pest Management tools and publish results in peer-reviewed journals. This position will be stationed at the USDA-APHIS Forest Pest Methods Laboratory (FPML) located in Buzzards Bay, Massachusetts, working closely with Dr. Miriam Cooperband at USDA-APHIS, in collaboration with Dr. Jennifer Hamel at Elon University and Dr. Rodrigo Krugner at USDA-ARS. Most work would occur at FPML, but the successful candidate would also travel to Elon University up to twice a year for field work and opportunities related to an academic setting. This position will support the training and development of a researcher with interests in insect communication and applied research. The successful candidate would work among a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technicians at the USDA APHIS PPQ FPML, gain experience investigating practical, real-world entomological problems involving important invasive species of insects, within a biosecure facility and in the field, and would also have opportunities to gain faculty- and student-facing experiences in an academic setting when visiting Elon University. Annual salary of $84,579 (Doctoral degree) or $69,905 (Master’s degree). This 12-month appointment has the possibility of renewal for up to three years. Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager Human Resources Reporting to the Director of Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, the Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager plays a pivotal role in ensuring the University's compliance with relevant Civil Rights laws and regulations (Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, ADA/504), policies, and training, with a specific focus on promoting fostering an inclusive and diverse campus community through training, outreach, and case management. The Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager is responsible for developing and implementing strategies, programs, and training initiatives related to civil rights and compliance with applicable laws and guidelines. The manager maintains confidential student and employee files in the university’s databases and serves as primary intake person in response to reports of sexual assault, sexual harassment, stalking, dating and domestic violence, and all other protected categories of discrimination and harassment. The manager is highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities; strong critical thinking skills; the ability to exercise good judgment and high levels of discretion/confidentiality; an intense focus on accuracy; excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 79fff449 Last Name (required) be152412 Email (required) cfc5e012 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/clinical-instructional-preceptor-physician-assistant-studies-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies",
      "description": "Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Academic Affairs Temporary Title: Clinical Instructional (Preceptor) - Physician Assistant Studies Position Type: Temporary Days Per Week: Varies Hours Per Week: VP Area: Office of the Provost and Academic Affairs Department: School of Health Sciences Position Summary Seeking qualified providers (MD, DO, PA, or NP) with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure PA students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments. Clinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in a variety of clinical settings. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Preceptor Benefits: • Payment is competitive and dependent upon the payment model of the preceptor's institution. • Cat 1 CME from AAPA for PA preceptors • Pipeline to future colleagues: Build connections and interview potential candidates for your job openings Minimum Required Education and Experience A relevant training degree is required. Must hold an active state license as MD, DO, PA, or relevant NP training and have at least one year of clinical experience. Physicians must also be board certified in their area of practice. NP example—a psychiatric mental health NP can provide a behavioral medicine experience, or a board-certified pediatrician can provide a pediatric experience. Required Other Training, Certifications, or Licensing Must hold an active state license and appropriate board certification as above Permission of the clinical site to host students (affiliation agreement required) Job Duties Clinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 1-2 PA students per rotation in obtaining clinical skills and medical knowledge to provide medical care in one of the following medical settings: -Pediatrics: 6-week experiences -Inpatient Medicine (hospitalist): 6-week experiences -Women’s Health: 3-week experiences The preceptor assesses student performance during clinical experiences using provided evaluation tools and provides constructive feedback for growth: -Demonstrates effective clinical skills according to evidence-based practices. -Serves as a professional role model for students and fosters a positive and -professional learning environment that respects diversity, equity, and inclusion. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 3f094603 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submi