    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/program-assistant-departments-of-computer-science-engineering-physics-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Program Assistant- Departments of Computer Science, Engineering & Physics",
      "description": "Program Assistant- Departments of Computer Science, Engineering & Physics - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Program Assistant- Departments of Computer Science, Engineering & Physics - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Program Assistant- Departments of Computer Science, Engineering & Physics position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Program Assistant- Departments of Computer Science, Engineering & Physics Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 University Administration Staff Full-Time Title: Program Assistant- Departments of Computer Science, Engineering & Physics Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: M-F Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: School of Engineering and Computing Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary The Program Assistant for the Departments of Computer Science, Engineering and Physics provides support to faculty, staff, and students within the three departments and coordinates day-to-day operations. This vital member of the Elon University School of Engineering & Computing interacts daily with students, faculty, and staff by providing clerical and office management support, by supervising student employees, and by providing written/oral communications to both internal and external audiences. The position also works closely with the Office of the Dean and other units across the University. To be successful in this position, the Program Assistant must possess the following qualities: • highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities • has a positive attitude that contributes to a collaborative culture • acts with flexibility and patience while remaining calm under pressure • willingness to learn new skills and programs • demonstrates good judgment and attention to detail • comfortable and confident working with students’ FERPA-protected information; • strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills • ability to work both independently and collaboratively, as part of a team on multiple projects simultaneously • proficiency with Microsoft products such as Word, Excel, Outlook, and Teams, also able to learn internal University platforms Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience HS Diploma and 2-5 years of experience in an office setting Preferred Education and Experience Associate's Degree (AA) in a related field and/or experience in education support, non-profit administrative support, other related field, or a combination of education and experience Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities A successful candidate will show evidence of: • ability to prioritize work according to departmental needs, can determine workflow problems and develop solutions, and efficiently execute workflows • proficiency with computer technology and Microsoft Office applications including Outlook, Teams, Word, and Excel • willingness/ability to learn new computer programs and software associated with administrative tasks at Elon • strong oral and written communication skills • professional and courteous manner and an ability to work harmoniously with other staff, faculty, students and other constituents. • exceptional time management and organizational skills • sharp attention to detail with the ability to multitask • regular attendance and punctuality • ability to independently plan, organize, and carry out work assignments • appropriate discretion when handling information that is both sensitive and confidential in nature Job Duties Administrative Support Collect, enter and update information in the university data systems Provide collaborative supervision for student staff members Support departmental hiring processes Plan and manage itineraries for interviewees, special guests, and other visitors Assist with the tracking and distribution of enrollment data Schedule room reservations as needed Participate as needed, in special department projects Attend and participate in staff development opportunities Communicate regularly with departmental faculty, particularly department chairs, to ensure timely handling of both regular and special departmental functions Communication & Event Support Assist with the planning and execution of departmental events Carefully prepare, review and edit various types of communications Assist with event and travel planning Financial Support Prepare check requests and purchase orders Assist in budget oversight, including monitor and reconcile expenses Manage procurement card expenses and allocations for the departments Process purchase, work, print, and catering orders; maintain financial records Community-Building Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Special Instructions to Applicants: Priority consideration will be given to applicants who have submitted their complete application, resume and 3 references with contact information on or before September 28, 2026. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert a5470a76 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) cc6b74a1 Last Name (required) af2b026b Email (required) 6e22b9ba Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university operations. The position also advances digital accessibility through resources, consultations, and support for accessible digital practices, and contributes to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular