    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/financial-aid-customer-service-specialist-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Customer Service Specialist",
      "description": "Financial Aid Customer Service Specialist - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Financial Aid Customer Service Specialist - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Financial Aid Customer Service Specialist position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Financial Aid Customer Service Specialist Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Finance Staff Full-Time Title: Financial Aid Customer Service Specialist Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Monday - Friday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: Admissions and Financial Aid Department: Financial Aid Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary This position serves as a primary customer service representative for the Office of Financial Aid. Primary duties will be the monitoring of the department email and fax accounts, answering telephones, working with students and parents in the front office and scanning, indexing, and maintaining the document imaging system. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience Associate degree, or vocational or technical school degree in any relevant field of study with minimum 1 year of experience with the following relevant work experience: Administrative support experience involving data entry, document collection, record maintenance, and use of computerized information systems such as MS Office. Preferred Education and Experience Associate degree, vocational certificate, or technical school credential in a related field of study. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong communication skills (both oral and written) to include appropriate tone, clarity, and timeliness. Willingness to learn and the ability to adapt to an ever-changing working environment. Exhibits a commitment to inclusive excellence through interactions with colleagues, students, and visitors. Job Duties Customer Service Monitoring and answering of FinAid email, FinFax transmissions, and FinAid Check Teams Group. Answering incoming telephone calls from students and parents. Assisting students and parents in the office. Answers questions regarding FAFSA filing, loan applications, adjustments to aid, requests for adjustment, verification, requested documents, etc. General Office Duties Scanning and indexing of important student documents into document imaging system and general maintenance and organization of system. Assisting with processes within the office as needed Office Support Assisting with training and development of student employees. Support all Admissions events as needed for our department. Other duties as assigned. Inclusive Community Building Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert bb868dce Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Financial Aid Financial Aid Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 804d9ba7 Last Name (required) 3d78d6be Email (required) 4bead2ab Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university operations. The position also advances digital accessibility through resources, consultations, and support for accessible digital practices, and contributes to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular travel between the campuses of Queens University of Charlotte and Elon University’s South End (Charlotte) is expected. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events at Elon University’s campus in Elon, NC is expected. Research Associate in Insect Vibrational Communication Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon University and the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) are seeking a Research Associate with a background in animal communication to conduct exciting, cutting-edge research on the invasive spotted lanternfly (SLF) (Hemiptera: Lycorma delicatula). The ideal candidate would have expertise in the study of vibrational communication (i.e., biotremology) or acoustic communication. Research will focus on elucidating the role of SLF vibrational signals in insect mate selection behaviors, aggregation, and other behaviors that may be exploited as pest control methods. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a team to develop vibrational signals into stimuli for novel behavior-based Integrated Pest Management tools and publish results in peer-reviewed journals. This position will be stationed at the USDA-APHIS Forest Pest Methods Laboratory (FPML) located in Buzzards Bay, Massachusetts, working closely with Dr. Miriam Cooperband at USDA-APHIS, in collaboration with Dr. Jennifer Hamel at Elon University and Dr. Rodrigo Krugner at USDA-ARS. Most work would occur at FPML, but the successful candidate would also travel to Elon University up to twice a year for field work and opportunities related to an academic setting. This position will support the training and development of a researcher with interests in insect communication and applied research. The successful candidate would work among a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technicians at the USDA APHIS PPQ FPML, gain experience investigating practical, real-world entomological problems involving important invasive species of insects, within a biosecure facility and in the field, and would also have opportunities to gain faculty- and student-facing experiences in an academic setting when visiting Elon University. Annual salary of $84,579 (Doctoral degree) or $69,905 (Master’s degree). This 12-month appointment has the possibility of renewal for up to three years. Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager Human Resources Reporting to the Director of Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, the Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager plays a pivotal role in ensuring the University's compliance with relevant Civil Rights laws and regulations (Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, ADA/504), policies, and training, with a specific focus on promoting fostering an inclusive and diverse campus community through training, outreach, and case management. The Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager is responsible for developing and implementing strategies, programs, and training initiatives related to civil rights and compliance with applicable laws and guidelines. The manager maintains confidential student and employee files in the university’s databases and serves as primary intake person in response to reports of sexual assault, sexual harassment, stalking, dating and domestic violence, and all other protected categories of discrimination and harassment. The manager is highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities; strong critical thinking skills; the ability to exercise good judgment and high levels of discretion/confidentiality; an intense focus on accuracy; excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 6a957be9 Last Name (required) 0dc5f528 Email (required) 392b3e9a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/associate-vice-president-for-student-professional-development-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development",
      "description": "Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Advancement Services Staff Full-Time Title: Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Generally Monday through Friday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: University Advancement Department: Student Professional Development Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary The Associate Vice President for Student Professional Development is a senior leader responsible for advancing the university’s mission through building, scaling, and sustaining high-impact employer partnerships that drive internships, experiential learning, and full-time employment outcomes for students and alumni. This position provides strategic vision and executive oversight for all career services functions, with a focus on employer engagement, relationship management, workforce alignment, and student career outcomes. The Associate Vice President is a builder who will serve as Elon’s chief architect of employer strategy, developing innovative, scalable partnerships that align academic programs with workforce needs, expanding meaningful experiential learning opportunities, and strengthening postgraduate employment success. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience KEY COMPETENCIES Relationship-building and business development Strategic, student-centered thinking Deep understanding of workforce trends and the recruiting landscape Inspired collaboration Systems orientation Management of multiple priorities in a highly-complex environment Cultural fluency Executive communication Commitment to excellence Preferred Education and Experience Bachelor’s degree required; Advanced degree preferred 10-15 years of significant leadership and progressive accomplishments in complex environments Demonstrated excellence in: Building best-in-class organizational relationships Recruiting, inspiring, and leading teams Developing strategy and animating action Driving measurable outcomes Job Duties STRATEGIC LEADERSHIP Position Elon as a premier talent partner for regional, national, and global employers. Develop and execute a comprehensive, data-driven employer engagement strategy aligned with the university’s strategic plan and centering on excellence in student outcomes. Build deep, long-term partnerships with employers by assembling a team that is externally focused Establish and deliver upon measurable, meaningful goals related to employer partnerships, internships, job placement, and career outcomes. Advise senior leadership on workforce trends, industry alignment, and career success metrics EMPLOYER AND INDUSTRY PARTNERSHIPS Build and sustain executive-level relationships with employers across key industry sectors. Leverage Elon’s alumni, parent, and donor networks to expand partnerships that generate internships, co-ops, research collaborations, on-campus recruiting, and full-time employment pipelines. Lead corporate outreach efforts, including targeted industry engagement strategies and employer advisory boards. Collaborate with campus partners to align employer engagement with corporate sponsorships and philanthropic opportunities. Promote equitable access to opportunities through diverse and inclusive employer partnerships. WORKFORCE ALIGNMENT Partner with academic leadership to align curricula with evolving industry needs. Identify emerging workforce trends and translate insights into programmatic opportunities. Develop sector-based career pathways and employer pipelines in high-growth fields. Facilitate employer input into curriculum design, credentialing, and experiential learning. OUTCOMES AND ASSESSMENT Establish and monitor KPIs related to job placement, internship participation, employer satisfaction, and graduate outcomes. Lead post-graduation outcomes reporting and ensure compliance with accreditation and regulatory standards. Use data analytics to drive continuous improvement and strategic decision-making. MANAGEMENT AND VISIONING Lead inspired planning aligned with the university’s strategic plan, Boldly Elon. Manage a team of 30 across three campuses, including six direct reports, fostering a culture of excellence, collaboration, and precision in execution. EXTERNAL REPRESENTATION Represent Elon at industry forums, workforce development boards, chambers of commerce, and other venues that elevate the university’s brand. Partner with the Office of Admissions to champion career outcomes for prospective students and families. Special Instructions to Applicants: ** This search is being conducted by The Duffy Group. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, current resume, and three references saved as one document, either Word or a PDF. The file name should start with your first name and then last name, such as, “John Doe - Elon Application.” This should be emailed to lpas@duffygroup.com with the email subject of “Application for Elon AVP.” Applications received through the Elon system will not be reviewed by the search firm. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert f1830f79 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 31256887 Last Name (required) bd32c955 Email (required) cad8045e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations.