      "description": "Clinical Instructor - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Clinical Instructor - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Clinical Instructor position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Clinical Instructor Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Academic Affairs Temporary Title: Clinical Instructor (30 open positions) Position Type: Temporary Days Per Week: Varied Hours Per Week: 12 VP Area: Office of the Provost and Academic Affairs Department: School of Health Sciences Position Summary Seeking qualified nurses with an interest and passion for assisting pre-licensure nursing students in developing clinical competence and critical thinking skills in a variety of clinical learning environments. Clinical instructors will facilitate and supervise up to 10 students per group in both the traditional and accelerated BSN students in obtaining nursing skills and nursing knowledge to provide nursing care in a variety of clinical settings. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience A Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) is required for this position. Candidates must hold an active Registered Nurse (RN) license in the state of North Carolina and have at least two years of clinical experience. Candidates will also be expected to enroll in a Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) program within five years of hire to support continued professional growth and alignment with department goals. Preferred Education and Experiences MSN preferred or enrolled in a graduate nursing program. Required Other Training, Certifications, or Licensing Must hold an active state license as an RN in the state of North Carolina Job Duties Clinical instructors will facilitate and supervise 6-7 students per group in both the traditional and accelerated BSN students in obtaining nursing skills and nursing knowledge to provide nursing care in a variety of clinical settings. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 9d7ac3b5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Health Sciences School of Health Sciences Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 0bdf01b6 Last Name (required) d5b4d269 Email (required) af1bb9af Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university operations. The position also advances digital accessibility through resources, consultations, and support for accessible digital practices, and contributes to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular travel between the campuses of Queens University of Charlotte and Elon University’s South End (Charlotte) is expected. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events at Elon University’s campus in Elon, NC is expected. Research Associate in Insect Vibrational Communication Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon University and the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) are seeking a Research Associate with a background in animal communication to conduct exciting, cutting-edge research on the invasive spotted lanternfly (SLF) (Hemiptera: Lycorma delicatula). The ideal candidate would have expertise in the study of vibrational communication (i.e., biotremology) or acoustic communication. Research will focus on elucidating the role of SLF vibrational signals in insect mate selection behaviors, aggregation, and other behaviors that may be exploited as pest control methods. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a team to develop vibrational signals into stimuli for novel behavior-based Integrated Pest Management tools and publish results in peer-reviewed journals. This position will be stationed at the USDA-APHIS Forest Pest Methods Laboratory (FPML) located in Buzzards Bay, Massachusetts, working closely with Dr. Miriam Cooperband at USDA-APHIS, in collaboration with Dr. Jennifer Hamel at Elon University and Dr. Rodrigo Krugner at USDA-ARS. Most work would occur at FPML, but the successful candidate would also travel to Elon University up to twice a year for field work and opportunities related to an academic setting. This position will support the training and development of a researcher with interests in insect communication and applied research. The successful candidate would work among a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technicians at the USDA APHIS PPQ FPML, gain experience investigating practical, real-world entomological problems involving important invasive species of insects, within a biosecure facility and in the field, and would also have opportunities to gain faculty- and student-facing experiences in an academic setting when visiting Elon University. Annual salary of $84,579 (Doctoral degree) or $69,905 (Master’s degree). This 12-month appointment has the possibility of renewal for up to three years. Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager Human Resources Reporting to the Director of Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, the Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager plays a pivotal role in ensuring the University's compliance with relevant Civil Rights laws and regulations (Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, ADA/504), policies, and training, with a specific focus on promoting fostering an inclusive and diverse campus community through training, outreach, and case management. The Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager is responsible for developing and implementing strategies, programs, and training initiatives related to civil rights and compliance with applicable laws and guidelines. The manager maintains confidential student and employee files in the university’s databases and serves as primary intake person in response to reports of sexual assault, sexual harassment, stalking, dating and domestic violence, and all other protected categories of discrimination and harassment. The manager is highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities; strong critical thinking skills; the ability to exercise good judgment and high levels of discretion/confidentiality; an intense focus on accuracy; excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) bf915ddd Last Name (required) 770cf7d4 Email (required) 59ddb9e0 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/facility-engineer-elon-university-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Facility Engineer",
      "description": "Facility Engineer - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Facility Engineer - Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Facility Engineer position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Facility Engineer Elon Campus, North Carolina, 27244 Facilities Staff Full-Time Title: Facility Engineer Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Monday - Friday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: Finance and Administration Department: Facilities Management Location: Elon Main Campus Position Summary Provides assistance to the various divisions in Facilities Management with engineering support for the management, maintenance and repair of campus facilities and infrastructure. Ensure oversight of technical designs for the department's repairs to building systems and small construction contracts; engineering support and assistance to the division departments maintaining the campus buildings' electrical, plumbing, heating/air-conditioning, and other systems; and provides oversight of Elon's energy management program and monitoring of utility usage. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience Bachelor's degree in mechanical or electrical engineering with more than 8 years of experience with the following relevant work experience: Mechanical or electrical engineering design or project management in large commercial or educational facilities. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Position requires a broad-based knowledge of all phases of major building design, construction, and maintenance methods with a strong background in mechanical equipment and HVAC systems, including energy management system interfaces. Knowledgeable in design and operation of building systems; specification writing and interpretation; construction budgeting and control; and a basic understanding of current federal, state, and local environmental rules, regulations, and building codes. Required Other Training, Certifications, or Licensing A Professional Engineer’s (PE) license is required. Certified Energy Manager, LEED, and/or PMP certification is desirable. Job Duties Responsible for the development of proposals, studies and engineering drawings for repair/replacement of mechanical systems in the areas of heating, ventilation, air conditioning, plumbing, and fire protection systems to support Facilities Management initiatives. Provides leadership and direction for the BAS Application Engineer, Maintenance Engineer, and Utilities Clerk in the operation, expansion and utilization of building controls, existing preventive maintenance program, and utilities billing. Serve as an engineering liaison to the University's Planning, Design and Construction for Facilities Management. Review engineering drawings and specifications, construction submittals, and other documents to ensure compliance with university standards. Responsible for the management of the Elon's Facilities Management technical library, plans/as-built drawings and university mapping. Maintain, monitor and manage all major equipment warranties. Serves as the University's Energy Manager, advising Facilities Management leadership of desirable energy conservation initiatives. Monitor and analyze energy consumption, budgeting and costs; oversee campus metering and energy monitoring programs; identify funding opportunities; and coordinate energy retrofit projects and energy audits, including a retro-commissioning/monitoring-based commissioning process for campus facilities. Inclusive Community Building Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility within our residential campus. All who work at Elon should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring and collaboration in a close-knit residential community. We embrace the shared responsibility to foster inclusive excellence within a strong residential community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus activities such as College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resource groups and other university-sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Special Instructions to Applicants: Emergency Operations Support Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert cded7d07 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Management Facilities Management Locations Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) f5de82d2 Last Name (required) fe54a8f7 Email (required) cfeffd8c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university operations. The position also advances digital accessibility through resources, consultations, and support for accessible digital practices, and contributes to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular travel between the campuses of Queens University of Charlotte and Elon University’s South End (Charlotte) is expected. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events at Elon University’s campus in Elon, NC is expected. Research Associate in Insect Vibrational Communication Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon University and the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) are seeking a Research Associate with a background in animal communication to conduct exciting, cutting-edge research on the invasive spotted lanternfly (SLF) (Hemiptera: Lycorma delicatula). The ideal candidate would have expertise in the study of vibrational communication (i.e., biotremology) or acoustic communication. Research will focus on elucidating the role of SLF vibrational signals in insect mate selection behaviors, aggregation, and other behaviors that may be exploited as pest control methods. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a team to develop vibrational signals into stimuli for novel behavior-based Integrated Pest Management tools and publish results in peer-reviewed journals. This position will be stationed at the USDA-APHIS Forest Pest Methods Laboratory (FPML) located in Buzzards Bay, Massachusetts, working closely with Dr. Miriam Cooperband at USDA-APHIS, in collaboration with Dr. Jennifer Hamel at Elon University and Dr. Rodrigo Krugner at USDA-ARS. Most work would occur at FPML, but the successful candidate would also travel to Elon University up to twice a year for field work and opportunities related to an academic setting. This position will support the training and development of a researcher with interests in insect communication and applied research. The successful candidate would work among a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technicians at the USDA APHIS PPQ FPML, gain experience investigating practical, real-world entomological problems involving important invasive species of insects, within a biosecure facility and in the field, and would also have opportunities to gain faculty- and student-facing experiences in an academic setting when visiting Elon University. Annual salary of $84,579 (Doctoral degree) or $69,905 (Master’s degree). This 12-month appointment has the possibility of renewal for up to three years. Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager Human Resources Reporting to the Director of Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, the Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager plays a pivotal role in ensuring the University's compliance with relevant Civil Rights laws and regulations (Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, ADA/504), policies, and training, with a specific focus on promoting fostering an inclusive and diverse campus community through training, outreach, and case management. The Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager is responsible for developing and implementing strategies, programs, and training initiatives related to civil rights and compliance with applicable laws and guidelines. The manager maintains confidential student and employee files in the university’s databases and serves as primary intake person in response to reports of sexual assault, sexual harassment, stalking, dating and domestic violence, and all other protected categories of discrimination and harassment. The manager is highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities; strong critical thinking skills; the ability to exercise good judgment and high levels of discretion/confidentiality; an intense focus on accuracy; excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 3c36b2eb Last Name (required) 3c100e36 Email (required) b6eeb379 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
