    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/associate-full-professor-of-law-queens-campus-charlotte-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor of Law - Queens Campus",
      "description": "Associate/Full Professor of Law - Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States Associate/Full Professor of Law - Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Associate/Full Professor of Law position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Associate/Full Professor of Law Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, 28216 Academic Affairs Faculty Full-Time Title: Associate/Full Professor of Law Position Type: Faculty Full-Time Days Per Week: Hours Per Week: VP Area: Office of the Provost and Academic Affairs Department: Elon University School of Law Location: Queens Campus - Charlotte Position Summary Elon University School of Law invites applications from faculty candidates with law teaching experience to join the full-time faculty at our new Charlotte location, which will welcome its first full-time class in August 2027. We are interested in faculty who can teach first-year courses. The positions will start in summer 2027. The success of Elon Law’s innovative, highly experiential, full-time 2.5-year curriculum has led us to open a second full-time law program at our campus in Charlotte, North Carolina.We seek a colleague who is eager to contribute to our mission: blending strong classroom instruction with experiential learning to fully equip a vibrant generation of practice-ready law graduates, while pursuing forward-looking scholarship and embracing excellence in teaching, mentoring, service and scholarship. Required qualifications include a J.D. or equivalent law degree, outstanding academic credentials, substantive practice experience, and admission with good standing to practice. To apply, please submit a current C.V., a statement of interest, and teaching/research agenda. For more information about Elon Law and Elon University, visit law.elon.edu. Benefits of Working at Elon Minimum Required Education and Experience J.D. Required; 3-5 years faculty experience Preferred Education and Experience Strong record of teaching and scholarly excellence, as well as a commitment to building out the Charlotte program. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Required Other Training, Certifications, or Licensing Job Duties Special Instructions to Applicants: Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert fba83900 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Elon University School of Law Elon University School of Law Locations Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 15d1d023 Last Name (required) 35d11130 Email (required) 3b0a4fbf Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississi