to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular travel between the campuses of Queens University of Charlotte and Elon University’s South End (Charlotte) is expected. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events at Elon University’s campus in Elon, NC is expected. Research Associate in Insect Vibrational Communication Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon University and the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) are seeking a Research Associate with a background in animal communication to conduct exciting, cutting-edge research on the invasive spotted lanternfly (SLF) (Hemiptera: Lycorma delicatula). The ideal candidate would have expertise in the study of vibrational communication (i.e., biotremology) or acoustic communication. Research will focus on elucidating the role of SLF vibrational signals in insect mate selection behaviors, aggregation, and other behaviors that may be exploited as pest control methods. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a team to develop vibrational signals into stimuli for novel behavior-based Integrated Pest Management tools and publish results in peer-reviewed journals. This position will be stationed at the USDA-APHIS Forest Pest Methods Laboratory (FPML) located in Buzzards Bay, Massachusetts, working closely with Dr. Miriam Cooperband at USDA-APHIS, in collaboration with Dr. Jennifer Hamel at Elon University and Dr