    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-law-queens-campus-charlotte-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Law - Queens Campus",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Law - Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States Assistant Professor of Law - Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Assistant Professor of Law position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Assistant Professor of Law Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, 28216 Academic Affairs Faculty Full-Time Title: Assistant Professor of Law Position Type: Faculty Full-Time Days Per Week: Hours Per Week: VP Area: Office of the Provost and Academic Affairs Department: Elon University School of Law Location: Queens Campus - Charlotte Position Summary Elon University School of Law invites applications for entry-level faculty positions to teach at our new Charlotte location, which will welcome its charter full-time class in August 2027. We are interested in faculty who can teach Business Associations, Civil Procedure, Contracts, Criminal Law, and Evidence. The positions will start in summer 2027. Elon Law is recognized for innovation in legal education through a highly experiential, full-time 2.5-year curriculum that has led to increases in applications, selectivity, bar passage rates, and post-graduate placement. We seek colleagues who are eager to contribute to our mission: blending strong classroom instruction with experiential learning to fully equip a vibrant generation of practice-ready law graduates, while pursuing forward-looking scholarship and embracing excellence in teaching, mentoring, service and scholarship. Required qualifications include a J.D. or equivalent law degree, outstanding academic credentials, substantive practice experience, and admission with good standing to practice. To apply, please submit a current C.V., a letter of interest, and a teaching/research agenda. For more information, contact the entry-level hiring chair, Prof. David S. Levine, at dlevine3@elon.edu. For more information about Elon Law and Elon University, visit law.elon.edu. Benefits of Working at Elon Minimum Required Education and Experience J.D. Required; 3-5 faculty teaching preferred. Preferred Education and Experience Potential for teaching and scholarly excellence, as well as a commitment to building out the Charlotte program. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Required Other Training, Certifications, or Licensing Job Duties Special Instructions to Applicants: Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 189a747d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Elon University School of Law Elon University School of Law Locations Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States Queens Campus - Charlotte, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 34967706 Last Name (required) 05888852 Email (required) efa63fd5 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university operations. The position also advances digital accessibility through resources, consultations, and support for accessible digital practices, and contributes to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular travel between the campuses of Queens University of Charlotte and Elon University’s South End (Charlotte) is expected. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events at Elon University’s campus in Elon, NC is expected. Research Associate in Insect Vibrational Communication Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon University and the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) are seeking a Research Associate with a background in animal communication to conduct exciting, cutting-edge research on the invasive spotted lanternfly (SLF) (Hemiptera: Lycorma delicatula). The ideal candidate would have expertise in the study of vibrational communication (i.e., biotremology) or acoustic communication. Research will focus on elucidating the role of SLF vibrational signals in insect mate selection behaviors, aggregation, and other behaviors that may be exploited as pest control methods. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a team to develop vibrational signals into stimuli for novel behavior-based Integrated Pest Management tools and publish results in peer-reviewed journals. This position will be stationed at the USDA-APHIS Forest Pest Methods Laboratory (FPML) located in Buzzards Bay, Massachusetts, working closely with Dr. Miriam Cooperband at USDA-APHIS, in collaboration with Dr. Jennifer Hamel at Elon University and Dr. Rodrigo Krugner at USDA-ARS. Most work would occur at FPML, but the successful candidate would also travel to Elon University up to twice a year for field work and opportunities related to an academic setting. This position will support the training and development of a researcher with interests in insect communication and applied research. The successful candidate would work among a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technicians at the USDA APHIS PPQ FPML, gain experience investigating practical, real-world entomological problems involving important invasive species of insects, within a biosecure facility and in the field, and would also have opportunities to gain faculty- and student-facing experiences in an academic setting when visiting Elon University. Annual salary of $84,579 (Doctoral degree) or $69,905 (Master’s degree). This 12-month appointment has the possibility of renewal for up to three years. Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager Human Resources Reporting to the Director of Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, the Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager plays a pivotal role in ensuring the University's compliance with relevant Civil Rights laws and regulations (Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, ADA/504), policies, and training, with a specific focus on promoting fostering an inclusive and diverse campus community through training, outreach, and case management. The Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager is responsible for developing and implementing strategies, programs, and training initiatives related to civil rights and compliance with applicable laws and guidelines. The manager maintains confidential student and employee files in the university’s databases and serves as primary intake person in response to reports of sexual assault, sexual harassment, stalking, dating and domestic violence, and all other protected categories of discrimination and harassment. The manager is highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities; strong critical thinking skills; the ability to exercise good judgment and high levels of discretion/confidentiality; an intense focus on accuracy; excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) faf9cf63 Last Name (required) 8ab4d7ad Email (required) 79f478a3 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/evening-and-weekend-reference-librarian-law-elon-greensboro-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Evening and Weekend Reference Librarian - Law - Elon",
      "description": "Evening and Weekend Reference Librarian - Law - Elon - Greensboro Campus, North Carolina, United States Evening and Weekend Reference Librarian - Law - Elon - Greensboro Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Evening and Weekend Reference Librarian - Law position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Evening and Weekend Reference Librarian - Law Elon - Greensboro Campus, North Carolina, 27401 Library Staff Full-Time Title: Evening and Weekend Reference Librarian - Law Position Type: Staff Full-Time Days Per Week: Sunday - Thursday Hours Per Week: 40 VP Area: Office of the Provost and Academic Affairs Department: Elon University School of Law Location: Elon - Greensboro Campus Position Summary The Elon University School of Law Library is located in Greensboro, North Carolina. The law library attempts to fully meet the educational and research needs of the Elon Law community, including students, staff, faculty, and adjuncts. The Law Library also serves as a source of legal information for the Elon Law alumni base, practicing attorneys in Greensboro, and provides limited services to the general public. The Evening and Weekend Reference Librarian – Law position is part of the law library staff of seven positions. One of the key responsibilities of this position is legal research instruction. The position requires co-teaching (and occasional individual teaching) in the library instructional program along with three other librarians, including the library director. In collaboration with the Acquisitions & Electronic Resources Librarian, this position oversees the library’s Federal Depository Program. Although infrequent, travel to and from Elon University’s central campus and Charlotte campus may be needed. All required travel and most travel for professional development is supported by the law library. Benefits of Working at Elon As an Elon University employee, you’ll join an internationally acclaimed university with a commitment to fostering a thriving community. Ranked among the most innovative, creative and best-run universities in the nation, Elon’s personal approach to education extends to employees, whose growth, professional development and success is a hallmark of our training and advancement opportunities. Elon University’s home is the charming town of Elon, North Carolina, a small, friendly community located a short distance from the beach and the mountains, and among the vibrant cities of Greensboro, Raleigh and Durham. In addition to the beautiful canopy of historic oak trees iconic to our campus, you’ll find boundless opportunities for family-friendly recreation, cultural events and outdoor activities. Hiking, water sports, fine dining and entertainment are just a few of the many happenings in the Elon area, making the region one of the nation’s premier travel destinations. Employees at Elon enjoy a generous and comprehensive benefits package that includes: 28 annual days off, including holidays and vacation. Immediate tuition remission for undergraduate courses Tuition remission for approved graduate-level courses after 12 months of employment. Retirement plan with an 8 percent contribution from the university. Immediate eligibility for health, dental and vision insurance, along with free acute care and lab services at our onsite Health & Wellness Clinic. Free use of campus fitness facilities. Free admission to musical and theater performances, guest speakers, religious and ethnic observances, recitals, art exhibitions, entertainment and our Division I Phoenix athletics. Eligibility for tuition remission at Elon for spouses, qualifying domestic partners and dependents begins at two years of service. After two years of employment, eligibility begins for participation in the Tuition Exchange, a national scholarship exchange program that enables dependents to enroll in nationally recognized partner colleges and universities. Elon values and celebrates the diverse backgrounds, cultures, experiences and perspectives of our community members. As an equal opportunity employer, Elon’s principles of diversity extend to race and gender identity, age, disability status, veteran status, sexual orientation, religion, and other aspects of one’s identity. At Elon, our employees respect human differences, passion for lifelong learning, emphasis on personal integrity and an ethic of service. Minimum Required Education and Experience Master's degree in Library/Information Science and Juris Doctor law degree are required. Combinations of education and work experience will be considered. All applicants must have a JD degree. JD holders without an MLIS will be considered if a candidate has library experience or qualifications. Desired 1+ years of professional library experience. New graduates encouraged to apply. Some flexibility in scheduling may be needed 2 to 4 weeks during the academic year. Summer months (June, July, and August) may also require some flexibility in schedule. Hours may change if the library is open for reduced hours. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Competencies: • Expertise in use of legal databases and conducting legal research. • Experience in teaching law students. • Growth-mindset with a desire to develop leadership skills. • Excellent customer service skills. • Strong ability to effectively and professionally communicate verbally and in writing. • Ability to self-start with a high degree of initiative. • Ability to work autonomously with onsite supervision and peer support available. • Strongly value team-building, collaboration, and inter-departmental relationships. • Demonstrate strong interpersonal skills and be willing to work effectively with others to achieve common goals. • Demonstrate flexibility to address the unique service and support needs of the environment. • Flexibility in scheduling and work hours. • Demonstrate excellent analytical and problem-solving skills. • Strong organizational skills. • Ability to work well under stress and to meet deadlines. • Ability to multitask and prioritize. • Positive attitude towards learning and using technology. • Ability to collect, organize, and analyze department data. • Ability to serve in a diverse and inclusively excellent environment. • Familiarity with Microsoft office software and basic office equipment. • Confidence in troubleshooting technology issues as they arise. Required Other Training, Certifications, or Licensing Job Duties Teaches in the Legal Research program and develops instructional material for both credit-baring and non-credit instruction. Teaching first year Basic Legal Research is a requirement of regular job duties. Other teaching may be required as needed. This program uses the co-teaching model, with some opportunities for individual instruction. Providing informal instruction to students, faculty, student groups, or other populations as needed. (Example: Providing a “how to select a note topic” presentation for Elon Law Review students). Working with our Charlotte Flex part-time program and full-time program to provide reference and legal research instruction. Collaborating with other reference librarians and the library director to create and update legal research instructional materials, with a particular focus on Artificial Intelligence developments. Other instructional duties as needed and/or assigned. Provides general reference and research assistance to Elon Law students and faculty. Staffing specified shifts for reference desk services and virtual/chat reference. Creating and updating legal reference materials (e.g. instructional infographics, LibGuides, etc.) Attending regular reference meetings. Collaborating on reference projects as assigned and as needed. Updating reference documentation including the reference manual and other processes or procedures. Creating passwords for public computer use and trouble-shooting technology issues with computer systems. Providing limited reference guidance to public patrons. Other reference duties as needed and/or assigned. Participates in the library faculty liaison program, acting as the primary contact for assigned law school faculty and adjuncts. Providing in-depth research assistance to faculty members. Training faculty Research Assistants. Creating subject matter bibliography. Creating and updating LibGuides to supplement faculty courses. Providing credentials and instruction for library database usage. Other faculty service duties as needed and/or assigned. Participates in assigned and voluntary library committees. Contributes to policy management and development in collaboration with other library staff. Participating in the library’s Collections & Acquisitions Committee. Participating in the library’s Student Engagement Committee. Participating in the drafting, updating, and maintaining of library policy documents with other library staff. Other committee and policy duties as needed and/or assigned. Serves as library’s primary contact with the Federal Depository Library Program. Working in collaboration with the Acquisitions & Electronic Resources Librarian to manage the library’s FDLP membership. Fulfilling all requirements per the FDLP, particularly completing the Biennial Survey. Keeping the library updated as needed with changes or developments to the FDLP. Participating in the North Carolina Library Association Government Resources Section. Other FDLP duties as needed and/or assigned. Inclusive Community Building. Community is foundational to Elon and a shared responsibility for all who work at the University. Employees should demonstrate an understanding of and engagement with Elon’s foundational commitment to relationships, mentoring, and collaboration in a closed-knit community. Accordingly, employees are expected to join together and build connections in activities that foster an active and engaged campus environment and engage in professional development to support the shared responsibility of enriching diversity, equity, and inclusion through meaningful relationships and mentoring at Elon. Employees are encouraged to, for example, attend or participate in campus events such as Coffee and Conversation or College Coffee, Numen Lumen, campus cultural events, athletic events, continuing education, professional development opportunities and trainings, employee resources groups, and other university-sponsored and/or Elon Law sponsored activities to demonstrate an active commitment to the Elon community. Attending at least 3 professional development sessions per year. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please provide a list of three (3) professional references. References will not be contacted without applicant permission nor prior to screening interviews. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 45ae58ac Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Elon University School of Law Elon University School of Law Locations Elon - Greensboro Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon - Greensboro Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) e05f0321 Last Name (required) 1564fbd1 Email (required) 9bee5e99 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (