    "https://jobs.elon.edu/jobs/adjunct-instructor-sport-management-department-charlotte-campus-elon-charlotte-campus-north-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department - Charlotte Campus - Elon",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department - Charlotte Campus - Elon - Charlotte Campus, North Carolina, United States Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department - Charlotte Campus - Elon - Charlotte Campus, North Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Job Description for the Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department - Charlotte Campus position. Review job description, requirements, and qualifications. Apply or register interest for the position. Adjunct Instructor, Sport Management Department - Charlotte Campus Elon - Charlotte Campus, North Carolina, 28208 Academic Affairs Adjunct Elon University’s Department of Sport Management in the School of Communications invites applications for an adjunct faculty member to teach Sport Sales and Promotion in the Study USA Charlotte program: The Sport and Community Experience in Fall 2026 (August – December, 2026). We are seeking an accomplished sport business professional to bring real-world sales expertise into the classroom. Charlotte is one of the fastest-growing sport business hubs in the country, hosting over 220 days of live sporting events annually. Home to the Charlotte Hornets, Carolina Panthers, Charlotte FC, NASCAR, and the ACC, the city provides an ideal environment for students pursuing careers in sport business, particularly in ticket sales, sponsorship, and fan engagement. This course prepares students to utilize ethical and effective persuasive techniques across a variety of sport job forms and functions. Students learn best practices for sales scenarios ranging from ticket sales to sponsorships; proven strategies for sales management and training; and how to successfully promote sport products across paid, owned, and earned media. The ideal instructor will draw on active or recent experience in ticket sales, sponsorship, or revenue generation to bring real-world application to the curriculum. Key Responsibilities Teach Sport Sales and Promotion with a strong emphasis on applied sales skills and revenue generation Integrate current industry practices, tools, and trends into coursework Incorporate experiential learning, including industry projects, guest speakers, and site visits Provide feedback on student sales presentations, writing, and professional development Facilitate networking opportunities between students and Charlotte-area sport industry contacts. Qualifications Required: Master’s degree in sport management, business, marketing, or related field Professional experience in sport sales, sponsorship, ticketing, or promotion Commitment to student-centered, experiential teaching Preferred: This course is best taught by someone currently working in the sport sales industry. Experience with CRM platforms (e.g., Salesforce, KORE, Archtics) Teaching or training experience Familiarity with the Charlotte sports landscape Program & Location This position is part of Elon University’s Study USA Charlotte: The Sport and Community Experience, an immersive program where students live, intern, and engage directly with the sport industry . Application Process Interested candidates should submit: A letter of interest outlining qualifications and relevant industry experience Curriculum vitae (CV) Contact information for three references Applications will be received on an ongoing basis and positions filled as needed. About Elon University Elon University is an equal employment opportunity employer committed to a diverse faculty, staff, and student body, and welcomes all applicants. Elon has built a national reputation as a premier student-centered arts and sciences university that values strong relationships between students and faculty mentors. Elon’s more than 7,000 students prepare to become resilient, ambitious, and ethical leaders, putting their knowledge into action on campus, in the community, and around the globe. Elon is ranked among the nation’s top universities by U.S. News & World Report, including No. 1 for excellence in undergraduate teaching for five straight years and No. 8 for innovation. To learn more, visit Elon University . About Study USA The Elon Study USA Program is designed to help students experience the diversity of cultures, worldviews, and environments across the United States. Each program includes place-based learning, internships, alumni support, and professional development, helping students build industry connections and practical skills. To learn more, visit Elon Study USA . Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 3f0035ed Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Communications School of Communications Locations Elon - Charlotte Campus, North Carolina, United States Elon - Charlotte Campus, North Carolina, United States First Name (required) 24c26862 Last Name (required) cdba5bf6 Email (required) 1b052ac1 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Texas Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Texas. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Oklahoma and Louisiana. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Dallas, Austin or Houston metro regions. Regional Assistant Director of Admissions- Florida Admissions The regional assistant director of admissions is responsible for all aspects of undergraduate recruitment for students from Florida. In addition, this role will also provide territory management for Mississippi, Arkansas and Puerto Rico. The regional assistant director gives university information to prospective students and families through various communication methods. The regional assistant director is also responsible for territory development, along with building and maintaining strong relationships with high schools, counselors, and being active in relevant regional associations. The position is an 11-month regional position, and the ideal candidate will reside within 30 miles of Miami, Tampa or Orlando metro regions. Construction Project Manager Planning, Design & Construction Mgmt. The role leads projects through construction and closeout, with particular emphasis on contractor performance, schedule management, cost control, quality, and timely resolution of construction issues. The Construction Project Manager proactively identifies risks and potential delays, coordinates timely solutions to maintain project milestones and support successful completion, and monitors contractor and design team performance against contractual commitments. The position also provides construction expertise during planning and design to improve constructability, phasing, procurement, and schedule performance. Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility Information Technology The Instructional Technologist – Digital Learning and Digital Accessibility supports the Hayworth Center for Digital Learning (HCDL) as part of Teaching and Learning Technologies (TLT), providing faculty- and staff-facing expertise in digital learning technologies, digital accessibility, and learning design. The position provides consultative support for Microsoft 365, Canvas (LMS), and other digital learning tools, helping faculty and staff use technology effectively to support teaching, learning, collaboration, and university operations. The position also advances digital accessibility through resources, consultations, and support for accessible digital practices, and contributes to evidence-based digital learning design support by developing resources and providing learning design consultations. This position is in-person based in Charlotte, North Carolina. It will primarily serve the Queens University of Charlotte campus in Myers Park and Elon University’s programs offered at the South End Charlotte campus, while collaborating with TLT and IT colleagues located in Elon and Charlotte on initiatives as appropriate. This position reports to the Assistant Director, Hayworth Center for Digital Learning on the Queens University of Charlotte campus. This is a one-year limited term position. Regular travel between the campuses of Queens University of Charlotte and Elon University’s South End (Charlotte) is expected. Occasional travel for professional meetings and events at Elon University’s campus in Elon, NC is expected. Research Associate in Insect Vibrational Communication Elon College, the College of Arts and Sciences Elon University and the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) are seeking a Research Associate with a background in animal communication to conduct exciting, cutting-edge research on the invasive spotted lanternfly (SLF) (Hemiptera: Lycorma delicatula). The ideal candidate would have expertise in the study of vibrational communication (i.e., biotremology) or acoustic communication. Research will focus on elucidating the role of SLF vibrational signals in insect mate selection behaviors, aggregation, and other behaviors that may be exploited as pest control methods. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with a team to develop vibrational signals into stimuli for novel behavior-based Integrated Pest Management tools and publish results in peer-reviewed journals. This position will be stationed at the USDA-APHIS Forest Pest Methods Laboratory (FPML) located in Buzzards Bay, Massachusetts, working closely with Dr. Miriam Cooperband at USDA-APHIS, in collaboration with Dr. Jennifer Hamel at Elon University and Dr. Rodrigo Krugner at USDA-ARS. Most work would occur at FPML, but the successful candidate would also travel to Elon University up to twice a year for field work and opportunities related to an academic setting. This position will support the training and development of a researcher with interests in insect communication and applied research. The successful candidate would work among a multidisciplinary team of scientists and technicians at the USDA APHIS PPQ FPML, gain experience investigating practical, real-world entomological problems involving important invasive species of insects, within a biosecure facility and in the field, and would also have opportunities to gain faculty- and student-facing experiences in an academic setting when visiting Elon University. Annual salary of $84,579 (Doctoral degree) or $69,905 (Master’s degree). This 12-month appointment has the possibility of renewal for up to three years. Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager Human Resources Reporting to the Director of Compliance and Title IX Coordinator, the Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager plays a pivotal role in ensuring the University's compliance with relevant Civil Rights laws and regulations (Title IX, Title VI, Title VII, ADA/504), policies, and training, with a specific focus on promoting fostering an inclusive and diverse campus community through training, outreach, and case management. The Civil Rights Compliance Training and Case Manager is responsible for developing and implementing strategies, programs, and training initiatives related to civil rights and compliance with applicable laws and guidelines. The manager maintains confidential student and employee files in the university’s databases and serves as primary intake person in response to reports of sexual assault, sexual harassment, stalking, dating and domestic violence, and all other protected categories of discrimination and harassment. The manager is highly organized and efficient with the ability to balance multiple tasks and responsibilities; strong critical thinking skills; the ability to exercise good judgment and high levels of discretion/confidentiality; an intense focus on accuracy; excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 2b03db37 Last Name (required) 69791139 Email (required) 25b80860 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
